-led boycott kept them from competing and the field was much weaker as a result. In their absence the favorites were Americans " [:a {:href "/athletes/77766"} "Valerie Brisco-Hooks"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/77788"} "Chandra Cheeseborough"] ",  who had won the US Olympic Trials, with Briscoe-Hooks second. In the final, the early leader was Britain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/68781"} "Kathy Smallwood-Cook"] ", but Brisco-Hooks took over at 250 metres, and maintained her lead to become the first woman from a non-East European nation to break 49 seconds. The Soviets sponsored a competing meet at around the time of the Los Angeles Olympics and Koch won that in 48.16, with the first five runners breaking 50."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "364"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/77766"} "Valerie Brisco-Hooks"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "51.42 (1 h4)"] [:td {} "51.14 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "48.83 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "370"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/77788"} "Chandra Cheeseborough"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "50.94 (1 h1)"] [:td {} "50.32 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "49.05 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "153"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/68781"} "K